description:
**File:** rust/lichen-rpl/src/multi_instance.rs
**Line:** 443

**Issue:** The `total_aggregated_routes()` method sums `routes_learned` (u32) values using `.sum()` which will panic on overflow in debug builds or silently wrap in release builds.

```rust
let mut total: u32 = peers.values().map(|g| g.routes_learned).sum();
if let Some(ref local) = self.local_gateway {
    total += local.routes_learned;
}
```

**Trigger:** If the sum of all `routes_learned` values exceeds u32::MAX (4,294,967,295), behavior depends on build mode.

**Fix:** Use checked/saturating arithmetic:
```rust
let mut total: u32 = peers.values()
    .map(|g| g.routes_learned)
    .fold(0u32, |acc, r| acc.saturating_add(r));
if let Some(ref local) = self.local_gateway {
    total = total.saturating_add(local.routes_learned);
}
```
